      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Symphony Nova Scotia |  Neon Dreams"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Presented by\n\n\nWith a string of impressive awards (including the ECMA's Group of the Year in 2025), gold and platinum singles, sold-out international appearances, and over 100-million streams to their credit, Halifax’s own Neon Dreams are alt-pop pioneers, drawing inspiration from diverse pop, rock, folk, electronic, dance, hip-hop, and reggae influences. Known for their high-energy performances and multi-instrumental prowess, they join conductor Daniel Bartholomew-Poyser (himself a huge fan of the group) for their orchestral debut with Symphony Nova Scotia.\n\n\n\nWATCH & LEARN MORE\nCheck out ITS ALL GOOD from the alt-pop pioneer group Neon Dreams.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/LABcg3EEwyw?si=UsL49RdMHDr5Gkd4"
      }
    ],
