    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPresented by\n\nWith a string of impressive awards (including the ECMA’s Group of the Year in 2025), gold and platinum singles, sold-out international appearances, and over 100-million streams to their credit, Halifax’s own Neon Dreams are alt-pop pioneers, drawing inspiration from diverse pop, rock, folk, electronic, dance, hip-hop, and reggae influences. Known for their high-energy performances and multi-instrumental prowess, they join conductor Daniel Bartholomew-Poyser (himself a huge fan of the group) for their orchestral debut with Symphony Nova Scotia.\n\nWATCH & LEARN MORE\nCheck out ITS ALL GOOD from the alt-pop pioneer group Neon Dreams.\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNeon Dreams: Frank Kadillac, vocals & Adrian Morris, drums\nDaniel Bartholomew-Poyser, conductor\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t"
      }
